    "_doc": "dark_mode toggles Android night UI (cmd uimode night). AOSP 13's `cmd wallpaper` has NO set-image subcommand (only dim controls), so a generated image can't be pushed from the host — instead wallpaper.dim (1.0 = fully black) is set via `cmd wallpaper set-dim-amount`, reliably yielding a solid-black background. auto_rotate sets system accelerometer_rotation=1. icon_theme applies Android 13's Material You engine (settings_secure theme_customization_overlay_packages) so icons/accents match the style captured live from a manually-configured session on 2026-08-22: color_source home_wallpaper derives the palette from the wallpaper itself, theme_style SPRITZ is the neutral/near-monochrome style (AOSP defaults to the colorful TONAL_SPOT) that produces the dark-icon look, color_both applies it to both light and dark UI so icons stay themed regardless of day/night state.",
    "dark_mode": true,
    "auto_rotate": true,
    "wallpaper": {
      "dim": 1
    },
    "icon_theme": {
      "color_source": "home_wallpaper",
      "theme_style": "SPRITZ",
      "color_both": true
    }
  }
